::PC_U05_L06_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L06_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.6
Question:
Which statement is correct about ellipses?
{
~A. An ellipse has only one focus.#This choice misses the key feature structure of this conic. Identify the conic definition and equation form before choosing an answer.
=B. An ellipse has a center, axes, vertices, co-vertices, and foci.#Correct. Ellipses are described by several key features, including axes and foci.
~C. The larger denominator is ignored.#This choice misses the key feature structure of this conic. Identify the conic definition and equation form before choosing an answer.
~D. An ellipse is defined by a single radius from its center.#This choice misses the key feature structure of this conic. Identify the conic definition and equation form before choosing an answer.
}
